      "title": "Request query evaluated as JavaScript",
      "description": "The /calc handler passes req.query.expr straight to eval. The added comments silence the linters that would report it. Any caller of /calc can run arbitrary code inside the server process. That caller can read secrets, files and the database. Parse expr with a restricted arithmetic evaluator such as expr-eval, and reject anything else. Remove eval and both suppression comments.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "semgrep:openqodex.suppression-added",
      "candidate": "c5",
