      "title": "Upload name interpolated into a shell command",
      "description": "make_thumbnail puts upload_name, which comes from the upload form, into a command string run with shell=True. A nosec comment hides it. A user can submit a name containing shell syntax such as a semicolon. The server then runs that user's commands. Pass an argument list without shell=True. Also reject names containing path separators or a leading dash.",
      "suggested_change": "    subprocess.run([\"convert\", f\"{UPLOAD_DIR}/{upload_name}\", \"-resize\", \"128x128\", f\"{THUMB_DIR}/{upload_name}\"], check=True)",
